---
/**
 * About — monolingual English page (ZH mirror at /zh-hant/about).
 *
 * Alternating background rhythm per 04-pages.md:
 *   canvas (Why) → warm (Believe) → canvas (How) → warm (Teach) →
 *   surface cream-mid (BC, emphasized) → warm (Who) → emphasis (CTA).
 *
 * The BC Benefit Company section is the page's anchor: cream-mid
 * background, terracotta pill stamp, terracotta-dot bullets.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '@components/Hero.astro';
import SectionHeader from '@components/SectionHeader.astro';
import CTABand from '@components/CTABand.astro';
import { CAL_COM_URL } from '@i18n/strings';

const principles = [
  {
    title: 'The process over the product.',
    body: 'We value the act of inquiry, wondering, getting stuck, revising, over arriving at correct answers. The answer changes. The habit of thinking well does not.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Love is infrastructure.',
    body: 'Students learn differently when they are deeply known and cared for. The relationship between teacher and student is not a soft benefit. It is the foundation on which all learning is built.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Human first, tools second.',
    body: 'Technology is welcome when it serves human development. It is refused when it replaces the struggle that builds understanding.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Learning is communal.',
    body: 'The word "collective" is deliberate. Education happens between people, not between a person and a screen, and not in isolation.',
  },
];

const benefits = [
  'Cultivating critical thinking in children, so they can participate thoughtfully in a world shaped by AI.',
  'Centering inquiry and process over product, building habits of learning that last a lifetime.',
  'Making high-quality supplementary education accessible to Chinese-speaking families in Canada, a community we know is underserved.',
];

const pageDesc = 'An education collective built to protect critical thinking in the age of AI. Registered as a BC Benefit Company with public-benefit commitments written into our incorporation.';

const hreflang = [
  { hreflang: 'en', href: 'https://forhuman.ca/about' },
  { hreflang: 'zh-Hant', href: 'https://forhuman.ca/zh-hant/about' },
  { hreflang: 'x-default', href: 'https://forhuman.ca/about' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description={pageDesc}
  chrome="mono"
  htmlLang="en-CA"
  locale="en"
  mirrorHref="/zh-hant/about"
  hreflang={hreflang}
>
  <Hero
    variant="mono"
    en={{
      headline: 'Human, is an education collective.',
      sub: 'What we believe, how we work, and why it matters.',
    }}
  />

  <section class="section section--narrow">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="WHY WE EXIST" title="The question is the point." />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          In the age of AI, the most important question in education has changed. It is no longer what children learn, but how they stay human while learning.
        </p>
        <p>
          When answers are instant, the muscle of struggling with a question, where real thinking develops, gets weaker. We started Human, to protect that muscle.
        </p>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="pullquote">
        <p>Education's purpose is not optimization. It is not scores. It is not AI-readiness. It is becoming more fully human.</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--warm">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="WHAT WE BELIEVE" title="Four principles we hold." align="center" />
      <div class="principle-grid">
        {principles.map((p) => (
          <article class="principle-card">
            <h3 class="principle-card__title">{p.title}</h3>
            <p class="principle-card__body">{p.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--narrow">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="HOW WE WORK" title="Small on purpose." />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We work one-on-one. A teacher holds a small number of students at a time, which means we can hold what each one is doing, where they're stuck, and what they care about. Progress in any subject is built on trust. Trust needs attention. That is what small numbers and one-to-one time buys.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every week, parents and students see a shared Kanban board. It shows what was worked on, what the student noticed, and what's next. No end-of-term surprises.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--warm section--narrow">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="WHAT WE TEACH" title="A liberal arts core." />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We teach English literature, writing, and critical thinking as a connected body of work. That includes close reading of literary texts, clear writing across argument and narrative, research habits that hold up past university, and discussion as a form of serious thought. We prepare students for specific tests when they need us to, and we coach university applications without ghostwriting. The common thread across everything: we teach students how to think, not what to think.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section bc-section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="bc-stamp" aria-label="Registered in British Columbia">
        <span class="bc-stamp__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="bc-stamp__text">REGISTERED IN BC</span>
      </div>
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="HOW WE'RE ORGANIZED" title="A BC Benefit Company." />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Human Education Collective Ltd. is registered in British Columbia as a Benefit Company. This is a legal commitment. We are required by our incorporation documents to operate for specific public benefits, not just profit.
        </p>
        <p class="bc-leadin"><strong>The three benefits we are committed to:</strong></p>
        <ul class="bc-bullets">
          {benefits.map((b) => (
            <li>{b}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p>
          We also commit to paying our teachers above market, because education depends on the people who do it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--warm section--narrow">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="WHO WE SERVE" title="Students who want to learn how to think." />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Most of our students are in elementary or secondary school, or at university. Some are in Canadian curricula, some in American, some in IB or AP programmes, some are new arrivals learning English as an additional language. What they have in common is a willingness to sit with a question long enough to understand it. We work best with families who value that kind of learning.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand
    variant="mono"
    en={{
      headline: "Want to see if we're the right fit?",
      sub: 'Fifteen minutes, no obligation.',
    }}
    cta={{
      label: 'Book a 15-minute consult',
      href: CAL_COM_URL,
    }}
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.section--narrow { padding-block: var(--space-16); }
@media (min-width: 48rem) {
  .section--narrow { padding-block: var(--space-20); }
}

.narrow { max-width: 48rem; margin-inline: auto; }

.prose > p {
  font-size: var(--fs-body-lg);
  line-height: var(--lh-body-lg);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  max-width: 62ch;
}

.pullquote {
  margin-top: var(--space-10);
  padding-left: var(--space-8);
  border-left: 3px solid var(--color-terracotta);
  max-width: 54ch;
}
.pullquote p {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 1.1rem + 1vw, 1.75rem); /* 22 → 28 */
  line-height: 1.4;
  font-weight: var(--fw-body-medium);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  font-style: normal;
}

.principle-grid {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--space-6);
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
}
@media (min-width: 48rem) {
  .principle-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-8); }
}

.principle-card {
  background: var(--bg-surface);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: var(--space-8);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-3);
}
.principle-card__title {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-h3);
  line-height: var(--lh-h3);
  letter-spacing: var(--ls-h3);
  font-weight: var(--fw-h3);
  color: var(--text-primary);
}
.principle-card__body {
  color: var(--text-primary);
  font-size: var(--fs-body);
  line-height: var(--lh-body);
}

/* ---------- BC Benefit Company section ---------- */
.bc-section {
  background: var(--bg-surface);
  padding-block: var(--space-20);
}
@media (min-width: 48rem) {
  .bc-section { padding-block: var(--space-24); }
}

.bc-stamp {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  /* Use the accessible terracotta so 11px bold white text clears
   * WCAG AA (4.6:1). Brand terracotta is 3.88:1 which only qualifies
   * as large text (14pt bold / 18pt regular +). */
  background: var(--action-primary-accessible);
  color: var(--color-white);
  padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  font-weight: var(--fw-body-bold);
  letter-spacing: var(--ls-label);
  margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
}
.bc-stamp__dot {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--color-white);
}

.bc-leadin {
  margin-top: var(--space-6);
  font-size: var(--fs-body-lg);
}
.bc-leadin strong {
  font-weight: var(--fw-body-bold);
  color: var(--text-primary);
}

.bc-bullets {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-4);
  max-width: 62ch;
}
.bc-bullets li {
  position: relative;
  padding-left: var(--space-6);
  font-size: var(--fs-body-lg);
  line-height: var(--lh-body-lg);
  color: var(--text-primary);
}
.bc-bullets li::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 0.55em;
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--color-terracotta);
}
</style>
